D1 - perception / body-update data race in CreatureSystem::step (Docs/PERFORMANCE.md, section 6.3).

Splits phase 1 of CreatureSystem::step into two parallelFor passes: first every animal's body
(updatePhysiology, updateInjuries, updateMemory), then every animal's perception. perceive() reads
other animals' health, fatigue and defence, which the old single pass could be writing on another
thread at the same time (ThreadSanitizer: Perception.cpp perceive() vs Body.cpp recomputeImpairment /
updatePhysiology), making N-thread runs differ from 1-thread runs from time to time.
Cost: one more parallelFor per step (Docs/PERFORMANCE.md, section 2.4). Changes trajectories.

Not applied: Source/NoctisCore/Private/Creatures belongs to another work stream. Made against commit
5eabfd4 (CreatureSystem.cpp blob bf18c48); also applies to the working copy of 16 October 2026, 04:30.
